# Quality requirements

{% callout type="info" title="About this chapter" %}
Make the quality goals from chapter 1 concrete with a quality tree and testable *quality scenarios*: stimulus, environment, expected response and measure.
{% /callout %}

## Quality tree

- **Availability**
  - Resilience of dispatch operations
  - Recovery after outages
- **Usability**
  - Operating the app while on the road
  - Offline capability
- **Modifiability**
  - Integrating new telematics providers
- **Data protection**
  - Deletion and anonymization

## Quality scenarios

| ID | Scenario | Measure |
|:---|:---|:---|
| Q1 | A cluster node fails during peak planning hours. | No interruption for dispatch |
| Q2 | Telematics is unreachable for two hours. | Route planning fully usable |
| Q3 | A driver confirms a delivery without network coverage. | Recorded in under 10 seconds, sent once connected |
| Q4 | A new telematics provider is integrated. | Effort of at most 10 person-days |
| Q5 | An erasure request under Art. 17 GDPR is received. | Completed within 14 days, logged |
